    "answer": {
      "short": "$P=\\left(\\frac12,\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)$, $Q=\\left(-\\frac12,\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)$, $R=\\left(-\\frac12,-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)$, $S=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2},-\\frac12\\right)$. Use $(\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta)$ on the unit circle.",
      "worked": "On the unit circle, coordinates are $(\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta)$. The diagram places $S$ in quadrant IV, so its directed angle is $330^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nP&=(\\cos60^\\circ,\\sin60^\\circ)=\\left(\\frac12,\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)\\\\\nQ&=(-\\cos60^\\circ,\\sin60^\\circ)=\\left(-\\frac12,\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)\\\\\nR&=(-\\cos60^\\circ,-\\sin60^\\circ)=\\left(-\\frac12,-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)\\\\\nS&=(\\cos30^\\circ,-\\sin30^\\circ)=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2},-\\frac12\\right)\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
